[b]Coffee to Austria at the game's default quantity: −£5.12K a week. At the quantity this mod picks: +£306.[/b] Smart Treaties shows what every goods transfer treaty earns or costs you, before and after you sign.

[h2]The game never tells you[/h2]

When you send goods, your treasury buys them in your market, sells them in your partner's market, and pays the shipping lane. That is money in or out every week, for years, and nowhere on screen.

[h2]Before you sign[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Predicted profit on every good.[/b] Each card in the goods picker shows its best weekly profit in green, so you see which goods are worth sending before you click one.
[*][b]A smart default quantity.[/b] Picking a good starts at its most profitable quantity, instead of the game's default.
[*][b]Three buttons under the slider.[/b] [b]Best[/b]: the most profit while your partner still accepts the good. [b]Max[/b]: fills their shortage without going over your surplus. [b]👍[/b]: the highest acceptance, at the lowest cost. Tools to Austria: the game's top of range is 2,330 units for −£37K a week, the 👍 button gets the same +12 acceptance at 264.
[*][b]Net under the slider[/b], live as you move it. Hover it for sale, purchase and shipping.
[*][b]"No shipping"[/b] when your markets border each other.
[/list]

[h2]After you sign[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Net per treaty[/b] in the outliner, with the total on the Treaties header.
[*][b]Net per good[/b] in the treaty panel. Hover for the full breakdown, shipping lane included.
[*][b](ST) Net treaty income[/b] in the treasury tooltip, next to the game's own revenue and expenses.
[/list]

[h2]Where the numbers come from[/h2]

Prices use the game's own price rule, at first-week prices. Signed treaties use the real shipping lane. A draft has no route yet (the game only picks one when you sign), so drafts assume a medium-length route. That is the one estimate in the mod; the draft's Net shows it with a ~.

[h2]No cheating[/h2]

Display only. The buttons set the slider, exactly as you would by hand. Nothing changes your economy, your treaties or the AI.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Game version 1.13.[/b]
[*][b]Achievement compatible.[/b]
[*][b]Save-safe.[/b] Add or remove it mid-campaign; it stores nothing in your save.
[*][b]Single-player.[/b] The treaty totals assume one human player.
[*][b]All eleven languages Victoria 3 ships:[/b] English, Français, Deutsch, Español, Português do Brasil, Polski, Русский, 简体中文, 日本語, 한국어, Türkçe. Terms come from the game's own text, but these are not native-speaker translations. Post a correction and it goes in.
[*][b]Conflicts:[/b] it replaces the goods transfer picker, the treaty article and influence cells, the outliner's treaty rows, and two lines of the treasury tooltip. Another mod changing those same pieces will clash.
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]

Post a comment with what you would want next. Which goods do you trade the most ?
